## DESCRIPTION
## Optimization with constraints
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Optimization with constraints')

## From HH #15.3 Example 4

################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML


A company has a production function with three inputs [` x,y, `] and [` z `] given by [` f(x,y,z) = 50 x^{2/5} y^{1/5} z^{1/5} `]. The total budget is [` \$24,000 `] but they do not necessarily want to spend all of it. The company can buy [` x,y, `] and [` z `] at [` \$40 `], [` \$12 `], and [` \$10 `] per unit, respectively. What combination of inputs will maximize production? Use software to solve the Lagrange system.

The maximum is at ([________]{Real(150)}, [________]{Real(500)}, [________]{Real(600)}).
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();